Z||000006||Archie||07-30-2001||10:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B>What do you have for springs in the back LT1 Chop top? To me it looks like it needs to be lower back there.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Can I answer this one Joel?<P>It looks like the car is on a slight incline. Look at the curb in the background, tall curb on left small one on the right.<P>After taking that into consideration, the car does have a "Rake" towards the front. Even after putting the V-8 in, it still sat too high, so I lowered it 1.5" all around. Even after the weight of the engine and the 1.5" lowering the rear is still a bit high. But I liked it like that.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000007||FLASHY||07-30-2001||11:02 PM||||OK I raised the car up a bit for Pontiaddict and I raised the wing for Cheever2. How's that?<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/too_low2.jpg"> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||07-30-2001||11:18 PM||||That looks pretty damn good... <P>Of course.. not to be too picky.. the roof has a slight downward slant towards the rear, looks a bit wierd.  Roofline should match up with the angle of the door  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  or maybe it's just me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000009||FLASHY||07-30-2001||11:26 PM||||I agree Standard. I'll see if I can change that for you too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Sheesh the things I do for you people. J/K<P>I like the way the blue chop top looks with the back low like the front. It would actually make the roof line even lower. Hard to believe it could get any lower.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lowchoptop2.jpg"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Pontiaddict||07-30-2001||11:31 PM||||Thanks Archie. I noticed the rake in some of the other pictures he posted, but this was the first picture I've seen of the car with a clear side view. I wanted to make sure it wasn't just because of how the other pictures were taken.<P>I could see why people would like the rakish look, but it's not my style.<P><BR>Flashy, I like the second picture better. The first one made the wheelwells look like bellbottoms. ||||reg||1
