Z||000015||FLASHY||07-31-2001||01:11 AM||||I was just foolin' around for fun. I love your car either way. By the way, you said there's barely any room to lower it as it stands...what do you mean? You can't be talking about the fender gap obviously. Is it because of the width of the tires?||||reg||1
Z||000016||LT1 Chop Top||07-31-2001||01:16 AM||||Yes to the width...<P>I think there is about 1/2" between the tire and the rear suspension.  I am not certain that the rear suspension is stock (coil-over??)...Archie, what is in there??<P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Slammed Fiero||07-31-2001||01:31 AM||||I have 255/40/17's and coil overs on the rear and my car sits a lot lower on the back than the Lt1 chop top.<P>Take off the rear struts , take the collar off (spring perch) , and put coil overs on the back. there will be no interference with anything.<P>Right now the front of my car is a little lower than the height of a popcan. The back is the height of a popcan. Very low , have to watch where you drive, I have ruined 2 sway bar bushings by hitting the fill caps at the 7-11. <P>other than that , just the usual scrape in and out of driveways.<P>I think lowering the Chop top will do wonders for looks , it looks jacked up right now. I had the problem when I went to 17's with regular lowering springs, the low profile tire gave the impression of a huge wheel well gap<P>as for the width between the tire and strut , it should be fine , even with the collar on , I could get my pinky finger between the tire and strut collar. 17" hi po tires have extremely stiff sidewalls and do not flex much at all. I have run 100's of laps and never had interference between the tire and strut collar.<P>But for the $199 it will cost for coil overs.. I would get them. Best thing I did for my car. You can also stiffen up that rear suspension. Most aftermarket lowering springs are build for looks. you want a good stiff spring in the rear and it will dial out a lot of the understeer. I run 325lbs rear springs , also have 375lbs I got for my 3.8 SC converison. not sure if the added stiffness is needed , but I want to play around with different rates.<P>JM <p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 07-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||LT1 Chop Top||07-31-2001||01:47 AM||||Slammed,<P>Thanks for the info...  I didn't know what to call the "collar" things, are they just there as a safty feature?  Is this a stock 87 GT part?<P>I would like to lower the rear, but then I probably would not be able to see out the back.  As it sits now...I look UNDER the rear spoiler to see out of the back.  Seems there is always a trade off.||||reg||14
Z||000019||chester||07-31-2001||07:27 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>I have 255/40/17's and coil overs on the rear and my car sits a lot lower on the back than the Lt1 chop top.<P>Take off the rear struts , take the collar off (spring perch) , and put coil overs on the back. there will be no interference with anything.<P>JM <P>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 07-31-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I'm running 245/40/17 rear and 215/40/17 front. A pop can WILL NOT fit under the car. About 1/2 inch too tall. RCC coil overs all around.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I do love the chop top!  Maybe someday (glazing into wallet full of cob webs   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">    <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension<p>[This message has been edited by chester (edited 07-31-2001).]||||reg||1
